{:edb/db-before-t 1332 :edb/db-after-t 1333 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534645 50 #inst "2026-10-12T05:50:57.706Z" 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186193206 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n\nII. $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A$\n\nIII. $∂A⊂A$" 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186193206 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 4}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n- $A-∂A=\\text{int}\\,A$\n- $∂A⊂A$" 13194139534645 17592186045417 false] [17592186240997 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2\\le x<0,\\,0<y\\le 1\\}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}},\\,0<y<1\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186240997 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2\\le x<0,\\,0<y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,,\\,0<y<1\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139534645 17592186045417 false] [17592186240997 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/4f/4f65a735e53130f633635fdfc8cd6de6c4fa39ed1fb7913ba9679bb07e73a6a0.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/c7/c76cea9b33420bf6c2e03d8eecb105003ce8b4e619063cbf2b7fccd5bc596cb2.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<1\\,\\}.\n$$" 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186240997 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/4f/4f65a735e53130f633635fdfc8cd6de6c4fa39ed1fb7913ba9679bb07e73a6a0.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/c7/c76cea9b33420bf6c2e03d8eecb105003ce8b4e619063cbf2b7fccd5bc596cb2.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-2<x<0,\\,0<y<1\\,}.\n$$" 13194139534645 17592186045417 false] [17592186278571 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<36\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\nII. $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n\nIII. $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186278571 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}<36}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" 13194139534645 17592186045417 false] [17592186281284 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4\\}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?  \n\nI. $∂A\\cap A\\ne ∅$\n\nII. $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n\nIII. $A=\\text{int}\\,A$" 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186281284 1071 "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?  \n\n- $∂A\\cap A\\ne ∅$\n- $\\text{int}\\,A\\cap ∂A=∅$\n- $A=\\text{int}\\,A$" 13194139534645 17592186045417 false] [17592186281303 1071 "![](images/84/84806884f843154c17c338eef0f50d83cae049aece675450e21e58dade6a9f34.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border: 1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAA}}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186281303 1071 "![](images/84/84806884f843154c17c338eef0f50d83cae049aece675450e21e58dade6a9f34.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139534645 17592186045417 false] [17592186281303 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/ce/ce268d8b396ea63227734c1edd6b876bb0fe9755fa12a3b75be90c6ef4af5af3.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/84/84780a84406a3fd0e281737b979887e0de6b1e9fe39d440f379fbb2b84e80a3b.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-1<y<0\\}.\n$$" 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186281303 1074 "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/ce/ce268d8b396ea63227734c1edd6b876bb0fe9755fa12a3b75be90c6ef4af5af3.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/84/84780a84406a3fd0e281737b979887e0de6b1e9fe39d440f379fbb2b84e80a3b.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-1<y<0}.\n$$" 13194139534645 17592186045417 false] [17592186430775 1043 #edb/ref 17592186430776 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430775 1043 #edb/ref 17592186430777 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430775 1043 #edb/ref 17592186430778 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430775 1043 #edb/ref 17592186430779 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430775 1043 #edb/ref 17592186430780 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430775 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430775 1045 "Interiors and Boundaries of Sets" 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430775 1046 #edb/ref 17592186430779 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430775 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430775 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048621 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430775 1053 #uuid "ae35b94d-2e76-5fcd-b627-6a9afdd973c8" 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430776 1058 #edb/ref 17592186430780 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430776 1062 #uuid "17d99301-dd16-5965-97b9-df38716417f5" 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430776 1063 #edb/ref 17592186281284 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430777 1058 #edb/ref 17592186430776 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430777 1062 #uuid "73729323-9be1-5e40-94b8-3eddef70b4a7" 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430777 1063 #edb/ref 17592186278571 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430778 1058 #edb/ref 17592186430777 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430778 1062 #uuid "992eb2be-3ddd-57bf-a76a-79f416d50e34" 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430778 1063 #edb/ref 17592186193206 13194139534645 17592186045417 true] [17592186430779 1058 #edb/ref 17592